* CONTROL, GREEN TODAY.  Alternative evaluation `( e1, e2 )` -- manual v3.7 p.99
* "Alternative Evaluation" + Appendix note 3 -- when the FIRST element SUCCEEDS.
* SCRIP lowers TT_VLIST as e1 alone, so this half has always been right; it is here
* so that the two RED siblings cannot be mistaken for "the construct is unparsed".
        q       =
        OUTPUT  = 'first-ok  [' (IDENT(q) 0, 7) ']'
        OUTPUT  = 'lit       [' (1, 2) ']'
        OUTPUT  = 'cat       [' ('p' 'q', 'r') ']'
END
